const i=[{slug:"how-to-choose-home-nurse",title:"How to Choose a Home Nurse: A Complete Guide for Families",excerpt:"Learn what to look for when hiring a home nurse — qualifications, verification, costs, and red flags to avoid.",publishedAt:"2026-07-01",author:"Ambimed Care Team",readTime:"8 min read",category:"Home Nursing",relatedServices:["home-nurse-services","patient-care-at-home","home-healthcare-services"],content:[{type:"p",text:"Choosing the right home nurse is one of the most important decisions a family can make when a loved one needs medical care at home. Whether it is post-surgery recovery, chronic illness management, or palliative care, the quality of nursing directly impacts patient outcomes and family peace of mind."},{type:"h2",text:"Check Nursing Qualifications"},{type:"p",text:"Always verify that your home nurse holds a valid nursing registration (RN/ANM/GNM) from a recognised nursing council. Ask for original certificates and cross-check registration numbers. Ambimed verifies every nurse's credentials before deployment."},{type:"h2",text:"Verify Background and References"},{type:"p",text:"A trustworthy home nurse should have cleared police verification and reference checks. Ask the agency about their screening process. At Ambimed, every caregiver undergoes multi-step verification including identity, police, and reference checks."},{type:"h2",text:"Match Skills to Medical Needs"},{type:"p",text:"Not all nursing needs are the same. Post-surgical wound care requires different skills than palliative nursing or ICU-level monitoring. Share your doctor's care plan with the agency so they can match the right nurse to your requirements."},{type:"h2",text:"Understand Pricing and Contracts"},{type:"p",text:"Home nursing costs in India typically range from ₹800–₹1,500 per shift depending on the city and care complexity. Get a clear quote before booking, understand what is included, and ask about replacement policies if the nurse is unavailable."},{type:"h2",text:"Look for Agency Support"},{type:"p",text:"The best home nursing experiences come from agencies that provide ongoing support — a dedicated care manager, 24/7 helpline, easy replacements, and transparent billing. This is what sets professional agencies like Ambimed apart from informal referrals."}]},{slug:"cost-of-home-nursing-gurgaon",title:"Cost of Home Nursing in Gurgaon: 2026 Pricing Guide",excerpt:"A detailed breakdown of home nursing costs in Gurgaon — shift rates, factors affecting price, and how to get the best value.",publishedAt:"2026-07-05",author:"Ambimed Care Team",readTime:"6 min read",category:"Home Nursing",relatedServices:["home-nurse-services"],relatedCities:["gurugram"],content:[{type:"p",text:"If you are searching for home nursing services in Gurgaon (Gurugram), understanding the cost structure helps you budget effectively and avoid overpaying. This guide breaks down current pricing, factors that affect rates, and tips for getting quality care at fair prices."},{type:"h2",text:"Average Home Nursing Rates in Gurgaon"},{type:"p",text:"As of 2026, home nursing in Gurgaon typically costs ₹900–₹1,200 for an 8-hour day shift, ₹1,100–₹1,500 for a 12-hour shift, and ₹1,500–₹2,500 for 24-hour coverage. Specialised post-surgical or ICU-level nursing may cost more."},{type:"h2",text:"Factors That Affect Pricing"},{type:"p",text:"Several factors influence home nursing costs: the complexity of medical care required, nurse qualifications (ANM vs. GNM vs. BSc Nursing), shift duration, whether equipment is needed, and urgency of deployment. Long-term monthly contracts often come with discounted rates."},{type:"h2",text:"How to Get the Best Value"},{type:"p",text:"Book through a verified agency like Ambimed for transparent pricing with no hidden charges. Compare shift options — sometimes two 12-hour shifts are more cost-effective than a single 24-hour shift. Ask about package discounts for weekly or monthly bookings."}]},{slug:"signs-parents-need-elder-care",title:"7 Signs Your Parents Need Professional Elder Care at Home",excerpt:"Recognising when ageing parents need professional help is difficult. Here are seven clear signs it is time to consider elder care.",publishedAt:"2026-07-08",author:"Ambimed Care Team",readTime:"7 min read",category:"Elder Care",relatedServices:["elder-care-services","caregiver-services","home-nurse-services"],content:[{type:"p",text:'Many families struggle with the question: "Do my parents need professional care?" The decision is emotionally charged, but delaying care can lead to accidents, health complications, and caregiver burnout. Here are seven signs that professional elder care may be needed.'},{type:"h2",text:"1. Frequent Falls or Mobility Issues"},{type:"p",text:"If your parent has fallen more than once, struggles with stairs, or avoids walking due to fear, a caregiver can provide mobility assistance and fall prevention support."},{type:"h2",text:"2. Medication Non-Compliance"},{type:"p",text:"Missing doses, double-dosing, or confusion about medications is dangerous. A caregiver ensures medicines are taken correctly and on schedule."},{type:"h2",text:"3. Declining Personal Hygiene"},{type:"p",text:"Noticeable changes in grooming, bathing habits, or wearing the same clothes repeatedly may indicate your parent needs assistance with personal care."},{type:"h2",text:"4. Social Isolation and Loneliness"},{type:"p",text:"Withdrawal from social activities, rarely leaving home, or expressing loneliness are signs that companionship care could significantly improve their quality of life."},{type:"h2",text:"5. Weight Loss or Poor Nutrition"},{type:"p",text:"Unexplained weight loss, empty refrigerator, or difficulty cooking meals suggests your parent needs help with meal preparation and nutrition monitoring."},{type:"h2",text:"6. Cognitive Changes"},{type:"p",text:"Memory lapses, getting lost in familiar places, or difficulty managing finances may indicate early dementia requiring supervised care."},{type:"h2",text:"7. Caregiver Burnout in the Family"},{type:"p",text:"If family members feel exhausted, resentful, or unable to maintain their own lives while caring for parents, professional elder care provides essential relief while ensuring parents receive consistent, quality support."}]}];function r(e){return i.find(t=>t.slug===e)??null}export{i as b,r as g};
